[{"learnocaml_version":"2","kind":"exercise","title":"Sum From-To","short_description":"A Beefed-Up Sum Function","stars":1,"identifier":"sum-from","authors":[["Max Kopinsky","max.kopinsky@mcgill.ca"],["Jacob Errington","jacob.errington@mcgill.ca"]]},{"id":"sum-from","prelude":"","template":"let rec sum (start : int) (stop : int) : int =\n  failwith \"TODO\"\n\n(* To make testing easier, define your helper function for sum_tr\n   here at the top level. You should change the names of the arguments\n   to something more descriptive. You can also add more if you want. *)\nlet rec sum_tr_go stop param1 param2 = failwith \"TODO\"\nlet sum_tr start stop = failwith \"TODO\"\n\nlet sum_nr start stop = failwith \"TODO\"\n","descr":[["","<h1 id=\"sum-from-to\">Sum From-To</h1>\n<p>In Wednesday's lecture, we looked at the function <code>sum : int -&gt; int</code>, such that <code>sum n</code> computed the sum of all integers from <code>0</code> to <code>n</code>.</p>\n<p>In this exercise, we'll beef this function up a little bit. Instead of starting from <code>0</code>, we'll take the number to start at as an argument!</p>\n<p>Both the start and end should be inclusive, so that <code>sum 6 7</code> is 13 and <code>sum 2 5</code> is 14.</p>\n<p>First, complete <code>sum</code> in any (recursive) way you please. Then, complete <code>sum_tr</code> in a tail-recursive style.</p>\n<p>Your helper function for <code>sum_tr</code>, <code>sum_tr_go</code>, should be at the top level to make it easier for us to check that it's tail-recursive. Since it's not local to <code>sum_tr</code>, you'll need to pass <code>stop</code> as an explicit argument in order to use it. We've prepared this for you in the starter code. Try to only use two additional parameters (for a total of 3).</p>\n<p>As an extra bit of fun, if you happen to know the \"trick\" for this function, you can implement <code>sum_nr</code> which must not be recursive at all. This is decent practice for writing more complex mathematical expressions in OCaml, but is less relevant to the course material. If you don't know the trick, don't worry about it.</p>\n"]],"prepare":"cjgN9o91DrVfod9AUIFpeiVKXkt+C5tS359TPmx=","test":"","solution":"","max-score":33,"depend":null,"dependencies":[]},null]